-- Scope: Native-text support at the grounding-judge and recipe-export boundary.
-- Excludes: A deterministic proof of semantic entailment or visual accuracy.

contract NativeTextEvidence {
    export_candidates: (records: Any) -> Any

    @invariant BindQuotesToPositiveSourceUnits
        -- Every supplied native-text evidence quote names a declared positive
        -- unit and occurs in that unit's original supplied text after whitespace
        -- normalization only. Empty/whitespace quotes, changed case/numbers,
        -- paraphrases, image transcriptions and generated answer/evidence text
        -- cannot replace an actual source-text match. Validate supplied quotes
        -- regardless of the candidate's modality label or presence of images.

    @invariant RequireNativeSupportWhenPixelsCouldConfound
        -- For text_only candidates with any image-bearing positive unit,
        -- require matching quotes covering every positive unit. Missing quotes
        -- or uncovered positives cause quarantine with a stable diagnostic.
        -- A nonempty native title is not sufficient to bypass this requirement.

    @invariant PreserveTextCompatibilityAndImageEvidence
        -- Candidates whose positives are entirely text-only may omit
        -- native-text quotes at this gate. Independent source assessment is
        -- still mandatory for verified export. Image-grounded
        -- candidates need not invent native-text quotes. The shared grounding
        -- prompt requests supporting quotes for every new text_only judgement.

    @invariant RetainSemanticJudgementAndProvenance
        -- The grounding judge must determine whether quoted native text supports
        -- every material answer claim without consulting pixels. Quote membership
        -- alone is not proof of entailment. Pixel-dependent support remains
        -- image_grounded even when some unrelated native text is present.
        -- Generated evidence is never authoritative source text. Preserve all
        -- existing query/grounding gates and original modality labels; quarantine
        -- failed candidates without rewriting or automatically relabelling them.
        -- Retain supplied quotes in the portable source-record judge audit.

    @invariant IndependentlyVerifyNumericEvidence
        -- The answer-blind source assessment directs independent reading of
        -- every needed number, date and table cell from the positive source, with
        -- row/column labels and units checked. Uncertain or unreadable material
        -- values are unsupported, not accepted by trusting generated claims.
        -- A prompt-contract test proves these instructions are present, not
        -- that a probabilistic judge always reads pixels or numbers correctly.
}
